<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Powertech yr headline share rises 50 pct.</title>
<headline>Powertech yr headline share rises 50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended February 28, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		56.0	  vs 37.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 18.0	  vs 14.0</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters forecast Powertech's earnings to rise by a consensus 18 percent, although pinning an exact earnings per share figure was problematic as last year's base was unclear.</p>
<p>They expected a dividend of between 15.9 and 17.2 cents with consensus at 16.7.  </p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  47.2	  vs 28.6</p>
<p>    Attrib		    78.77	 vs 60.91</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   141.40	vs 91.43</p>
<p>    Tax			 60.30	 vs 40.29</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   3.96	  vs 18.38</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,814.24    vs 2,158.32</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  1.19	  vs 0.47</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     26.17	 vs 8.66</p>
<p>Div payable June 2</p>
<p>on register May 23</p>
<p>Full name: Power Technologies Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said exeptional items included factory closures, property devaluation, discontinued operations of Gentech Ltd which was sold off, the discount/premium on operations acquired and the surplus on the disposal of others.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
